RECORDED AS BRAINSTORMING. @ajs, 2026-10-21: "Anything we can take from https://arxiv.org/html/2609.40169v1 ...", then "could the skills/tools that reflow2 has be improved by anything in this paper? ... I don't make changes in reflow2 for the sake of itself, but to improve its usage as a design tool". Paper: Yang, Lai, Wang, Harari, Gabrilovich, Chang, "Learning from Research: Toward Lifelong Agent Harness Evolution" (read through a summarizer, main text only; the appendix's failure taxonomy was not read).

OPTIONS, sorted by his line of 2026-10-17 (reflow2 records, checks structure and computes; the agent proposes and explores; the owner decides):
(A) a check run on the data that shaped the design reads as tuned (from the paper's D_evo / D_val / D_test split);
(B) a choice made on a measured comparison says whether the difference is real (from its L_α > 0 retention rule);
(C) parts changed together get checked together: when one increment changes parts that share an interface, flag the lack of a combined check (from its finding that module gains were not additive: combined beat the best single by 3.5–12 points);
(D) a finding says whether it is the design's fault or the environment's, and how often it recurred; only recurring own-fault findings surface as gaps (from its failure audit);
(E) a skill step for adopting a technique from a paper, shaped like its "mutation blueprint": source as graded evidence, assumptions as premises, target part, interfaces, kept state, when it stops.
Not offered again: distinct approach families first (10-17's option (b), considered and not chosen; the paper's topic-coverage ablation, +1.4–2.3 points over relevance ranking, is new evidence for it, but it remains the agent's creative work).
